      "writtenOn": "2019-08-15T07:37:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Previous, I like Daichi\u0027s design. Looking the code again. Now I prefer Jean\u0027s suggestion. Not only for code simplicity. More important is that I found this change would let tethering flow be different between single downstream and multiple downstreams. See below case:\nON/OFF hotspot:\nTethering Master state machine: initial --hotspot ON:#clearTetheringDownstream()--\u003e Alive --hotspot OFF:#handleInterfaceServingStateInactive()--\u003e initial\n\nTurn ON usb tethering, then ON/OFF hotspot\n1. USB tethering ON so, state machine already going from initial to alive.\n2. Hotspot ON/OFF would be : alive --hotspot ON:#handleInterfaceServingStateInactive()--\u003e alive --hotsopt OFF:#handleInterfaceServingStateInactive--\u003e initial",
